+#### Current Player colour-token architecture
+
+The Player light theme uses OKLCH as the canonical colour representation. Its primitive palettes follow a
+Radix-inspired 12-step functional progression: low steps support application and component surfaces, middle steps
+support interaction and boundaries, and high steps support solid emphasis and readable content. Radix supplies the
+scale philosophy only; TeaseScript does not depend on Radix Colors, Radix Primitives, React, or generated Radix CSS.
+
+Player component CSS consumes semantic tokens, not primitive step numbers. The dependency direction is therefore
+`OKLCH primitive -> semantic token -> component`. The neutral scale keeps one additional
+`--neutral-disabled-text` primitive because the approved light palette has a distinct disabled/subtle-text anchor that
+would otherwise force one of the 12 functional scale positions to change meaning. This preserves the approved colour
+instead of inventing another near-duplicate scale step.
+
+The current approved light-theme anchors are:
+
