+
+The HEX values are compatibility/reference values only; they are not the canonical design source. The remaining
+primitive accent steps complete the functional 12-step scale and need not be used merely because they exist. Default
+neutral controls use `border-subtle`, hover can use `border-interactive`, and pressed or deliberately strong neutral
+emphasis can use `border-strong`. Application accent tokens remain separate from speaker, package, and media identity
+colours.
+
+A future universal dark theme should define a deliberately designed dark primitive palette and semantic mappings under
+`[data-theme="dark"]`; component CSS should remain unchanged. Do not generate dark mode by automatically inverting the
+light scale. The current task has no approved dark palette, so only the light mapping is defined.
+
